hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27599","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Habib ibn Zayd, from their freedwoman Layla, from her aunt Umm Umarah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon her - he said: and men of her people gathered to her - he said: She offered them dates and they ate, and a man among them withdrew. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is his matter? He said: I am fasting. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Verily, there is no fasting person with whom breakers of fast eat except the angels pray upon him until they rise."
"27600","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, he said: Habib al-Ansari narrated to me, from Layla, from her grandmother Umm Umarah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon her and she offered him food. He said: Come near and eat. She said: I am fasting. He said: When food is eaten with the fasting person, the angels pray upon him."
"27601","Haddathana Hashim ibn al-Qasim, he said: Haddathana Shu'bah, from Habib al-Ansari, he said: I heard a freedwoman of ours called Layla narrating from her grandmother Umm Umarah bint Ka'b that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon her and she invited him to food, and he said to her: Eat, and she said: I am fasting, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When food is eaten in the presence of the fasting person, the angels pray for him until they finish, and perhaps he said: until they finish their food."
